        "content": "<p><strong>From:</strong> Qiyuan XU &lt;<a href=\"mailto:cl-isabelle-users@lists.cam.ac.uk\">cl-isabelle-users@lists.cam.ac.uk</a>&gt;</p>\n<p>Dear Isabelle users</p>\n<p>I’ve written a patch for this issue and uploaded it to my conda channel. If this issue affects you, you can install the patched version with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Isabelle\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">conda</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">create</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">&lt;env</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">name&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">//conda.qiyuan.me</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isabelle</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">bicompose</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">rename</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"k\">fix</span>\n<span class=\"n\">conda</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">activate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">&lt;env</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">name&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"n\">isabelle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">jedit</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(Replace &lt;env-name&gt; with any environment name you like.)<br>\n<code>isabelle-bicompose-rename-fix</code> is a separate package built on top of the package <code>isabelle</code> which contains the original, unmodified Isabelle. To revert to the original version at any time, simply run<code>conda remove isabelle-bicompose-rename-fix</code></p>\n<p>Alternatively, if you’d prefer to apply the fix yourself, the patch is below:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Isabelle\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">---</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a/src/Pure/thm.ML</span>\n<span class=\"o\">+++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b/src/Pure/thm.ML</span>\n<span class=\"n\">@@</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">2578</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"n\">2578</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">@@</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bicompose_aux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opt_ctxt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ow\">{</span><span class=\"n\">flatten</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">match</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">incremented</span><span class=\"ow\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">state</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stpairs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">newAs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">As0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dpairs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tpairs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">As1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rder'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">         </span><span class=\"kp\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lifted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n\n<span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rename_bvars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dpairs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tpairs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">As0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span>\n<span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rename_bvars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dpairs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">rtpairs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">@</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tpairs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">As0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span>\n<span class=\"w\">             </span><span class=\"n\">SOME</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">               </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">proof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Same.commit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Proofterm.map_proof_terms_same</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p;</span>\n\n<span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"kp\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">strip_apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Same.commit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">As0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv_rule1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">proof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rder</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\">              </span><span class=\"kp\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">strip_apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Same.commit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bi</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">As0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deriv_rule1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">proof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rder</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"w\">           </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NONE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">As0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rder</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">         </span><span class=\"n\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">As0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rder</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"n\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"kp\">in</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Best wishes<br>\nQiyuan</p>\n<hr>\n<p>发件人: <a href=\"mailto:cl-isabelle-users-request@lists.cam.ac.uk\">cl-isabelle-users-request@lists.cam.ac.uk</a> &lt;<a href=\"mailto:cl-isabelle-users-request@lists.cam.ac.uk\">cl-isabelle-users-request@lists.cam.ac.uk</a>&gt; 代表 Makarius &lt;<a href=\"mailto:makarius@sketis.net\">makarius@sketis.net</a>&gt;<br>\n发送时间: 2026年10月28日 3:35<br>\n收件人: <a href=\"mailto:kevin.kappelmann@tum.de\">kevin.kappelmann@tum.de</a> &lt;<a href=\"mailto:kevin.kappelmann@tum.de\">kevin.kappelmann@tum.de</a>&gt;; <a href=\"mailto:cl-isabelle-users@lists.cam.ac.uk\">cl-isabelle-users@lists.cam.ac.uk</a> &lt;<a href=\"mailto:cl-isabelle-users@lists.cam.ac.uk\">cl-isabelle-users@lists.cam.ac.uk</a>&gt;<br>\n主题: Re: [isabelle] Soundness-critical issues in thm.ML</p>\n<p>[Alert: Non-NTU Email] Be cautious before clicking any link or attachment.<br>\nOn 27/10/2026 09:38, Kevin Kappelmann (via cl-isabelle-users Mailing List) wrote:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fabian Huch and I recently discovered some soundness-critical issues (attached<br>\nbelow) in thm.ML with the help of AI agents(*).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thanks for the concrete example, to substantiate what I said on a realated<br>\nthread \"MCP resources bounds\" (Sep-2026):</p>\n<p>On 08/09/2026 17:57, Makarius wrote:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There is indeed a fundamental problem here, because the MCP violates<br>\nlongstanding assumptions about how the prover works, and is used by a human<br>\nuser. So any \"mitigation\" can only be symbolic, not really a proper solution.</p>\n<p>At FLoC 2026 in Lisbon, I've had some discussions with users of AI + MCP. My<br>\nconclusion: we should gradually make the system more robust [...]</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Makarius</p>\n<hr>\n<p>CONFIDENTIALITY: This email is intended solely for the person(s) named and may be confidential and/or privileged. If you are not the intended recipient, please delete it, notify us and do not copy, use, or disclose its contents.<br>\nTowards a sustainable earth: Print only when necessary. Thank you.</p>",
